The new checkpoint validation in PR #2 at `aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0` rejects a checkpoint that the same engine successfully writes when a supported custom `RlmModel` returns an empty string. A subsequent valid finish can return success, but replay and resume both fail with `RlmError { code: 'incomplete', message: 'Run checkpoint is invalid' }`. An interrupted run with the same recorded empty-response refusal also cannot resume.

## Contract and cause

- [README](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/README.md#L80-L90) explicitly supports implementing `RlmModel` and says invalid JSON becomes a recorded refusal that spends a reserved step
- [The engine](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/src/engine.ts#L141-L164) accepts string response text, including `''`, checkpoints it, and records `{ refused: 'invalid' }` after JSON parsing fails
- [The new loader](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0/src/ledger.ts#L78-L86) calls `text(response.text)`, which requires a nonempty string. It therefore classifies this engine-generated checkpoint as corrupt

This affects the documented third-party model interface. The built-in HTTP adapter already rejects empty model text before writing it, so this is not a claim that ordinary Ollama/OpenAI-compatible runs necessarily hit the problem.

## Minimal regression

Save this as a test under `test/` and run it with Node's test runner in the project checkout:

```ts
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { test } from 'node:test';
import { runRlm, replayRlm, resumeRlm } from '../src/engine.ts';
import { tracker, ScriptedModel } from './helpers.ts';

test('empty model output remains a replayable refusal', async t => {
  const { workspace } = await tracker(t);
  const model = new ScriptedModel((_request, index) =>
    index === 0 ? '' : '{"action":"finish","answer":"ok"}');
  const result = await runRlm('Recover from invalid JSON', { workspace, model });
  assert.equal(result.answer, 'ok');
  assert.equal(model.requests.length, 2);
  assert.equal((await replayRlm(workspace, result.run)).answer, 'ok');
  const noInference = new ScriptedModel(() => {
    throw new Error('Completed resume must not infer');
  });
  assert.equal((await resumeRlm(workspace, result.run, noInference)).answer, 'ok');
  assert.equal(noInference.requests.length, 0);
});
```

## Independent verification

Using Node 24.19.0, unchanged locked dependencies and real SDK scratch trackers, four contract cases were tested on exact source:

- Prior head `76a20eb8d1920258dd3218d76f91147484406539`: 4/4 pass
- New head `aa3787b2c1a2d66ed784a4b0d824eb7341581bc0`: 2/4 pass; the completed and interrupted empty-response cases fail
- Controls with nonempty malformed JSON (`'{'`) and whitespace (`' '`) pass on the new head
- A separate diagnostic copy changing only response-text validation to accept strings, including empty strings, passes 4/4; its existing round-2 malformed-checkpoint/settings suite still passes 6/6

The new head's existing 91-test suite passes, so this edge case is currently uncovered. No external model calls or production data were used.

Please align loaded response-text validation with the writer and the documented malformed-action recovery semantics, preserving rejection of non-string response values. Keep a regression for both completed replay/resume and interrupted recovery. This is distinct from repaired issue #4 (failed recursive children) and the existing interrupted-spawn observation review thread: the minimal reproduction has one root call, and fails in `load` before replay traverses any action.
